<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="258" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Stamp BFF startup settings: the four keys a stamp's BFF demands at start but no channel writes (204e F5–F8)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — T186 blocker found by task 204e</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes what H4b writes to every customer stamp's BFF; a wrong value stops the BFF from starting.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Startup-validation semantics + the manifest/generator contract.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml + generated outputs, which T253 also edits — run after T253 merges.</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, bff-api, config, testing</tags>
    <deps>253, 204e</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Task 204e's IOptionsDriftTests found BFF options types whose startup validation demands keys that neither the canonical manifest (H4b) nor customer.bicep writes to a stamp. The dev BFF works only because these were set by hand on spaarke-bff-dev (verified 2026-10-09: Graph__Scopes__0, ServiceBus__QueueName, PublicConfig__BffUrl / MsalClientId / TenantId, Onboarding__EnableDevBypass). A T186 stamp would not start.</prompt>

  <goal>Every key a stamp BFF's ValidateOnStart options demand outside Development has a stamp channel (manifest per_env_settings or a secret with a KV reference); IOptionsDriftTests' KnownDrift rows 204e-F5..F8 become Supplied (or Exempt with the gate that is off on every stamp) and the ledger rows are deleted.</goal>

  <context>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Endpoints/Onboarding/OnboardingOptions.cs (+ its validator / OnboardingModule)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/PublicConfigOptions.cs (+ its IValidateOptions)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/GraphOptions.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/ServiceBusOptions.cs</file>
      <file>scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml (per_env_settings; PerEnvSourceCatalog) + its generator and generated outputs</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep</file>
      <file>tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/IOptionsDriftTests.cs (Census / KnownDrift ledger)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="bff-extensions F.5">Never weaken a validator to make a stamp start; supply the key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="provisioning.md">Keyless stamps (D13): a demanded secret (Onboarding HMAC key?) goes through the stamp vault as a KV reference — first decide whether a stamp needs that endpoint at all (needed → build, else gate it off with an Exempt row).</constraint>
    <constraint source="live">No live change; values derive from run context (BFF URL, BFF app id, tenant id) or constants.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">For each of F5..F8 read the validator: which key, demanded when, what value a stamp needs (and where the run context already holds it).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the manifest entries (per_env_source from the closed catalog, or a new source wired through HandlerRunInputs if none fits); regenerate.</step>
    <step order="3">Move the IOptionsDriftTests rows to Supplied / Exempt; delete the KnownDrift rows; tests green.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">IOptionsDriftTests has no KnownDrift row for Onboarding, PublicConfig, Graph:Scopes or ServiceBus:QueueName.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H4b's generated settings for a stamp include each demanded key with a stamp-correct value (unit test on the generated set).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Solution build 0 errors; ControlPlane tests and ArchTests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
